Reach the main screen through the live dock API instead of the deprecated one.

GameViewPluginBase::_focus_another_editor() restores the previously focused
main-screen editor when the embedded game window is closed.  It does so through
EditorInterface::set_main_screen_editor(), which is declared and defined only
inside #ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED (editor/editor_interface.h,
editor/editor_interface.cpp), while the caller carries no guard, so building
with deprecated=no (USE=-deprecated, -DDISABLE_DEPRECATED) fails with:

    editor/run/game_view_plugin.cpp:1855:59: error: 'class EditorInterface' has
        no member named 'set_main_screen_editor'

Unlike EditorMainScreen::add_main_plugin() -- see the companion patch
godot-4.8-disable-deprecated-main-screen.patch, where no non-deprecated
equivalent exists and the call has to be compiled out -- this one has a live
replacement, so the call is rewritten rather than guarded.  The three lines
substituted here are exactly the body of set_main_screen_editor():

    EditorDock *dock = EditorNode::get_singleton()->get_editor_main_screen()
                           ->get_dock_by_name(p_name);
    ERR_FAIL_NULL_MSG(dock, "The editor name '" + p_name + "' was not found.");
    EditorDockManager::get_singleton()->focus_dock(dock);

Every symbol it needs is available in both configurations:
EditorNode::get_editor_main_screen() (editor/editor_node.h, static),
DockTabContainer::get_dock_by_name() (editor/docks/dock_tab_container.h),
EditorDockManager::get_dock_by_name()/focus_dock()
(editor/docks/editor_dock_manager.h) -- none sit under a guard.  All four
headers are already included by game_view_plugin.cpp, so no new include is
needed.  ERR_FAIL_NULL_MSG returns from a void function either way, and the
call was the last statement on that branch, so control flow is unchanged.

Note that EditorInterface::get_dock_by_name() would NOT be equivalent: it
forwards to EditorDockManager and therefore searches every dock, whereas the
deprecated method looks only among the main screen's own docks.  Inlining the
original body keeps that narrower lookup.

Deliberately unconditional: the rewritten code compiles and behaves identically
with deprecated=yes, so it needs no #ifdef, and it keeps working once upstream
drops the deprecated method entirely.  Not an upstream mirror -- master still
carries the same call and no issue or PR covers it; recheck on every bump.

Corrected 2026-09-04: the two sentences above were true when written and are
not now. Upstream commit 2e26ab8a3afb ("Fix deprecated build after dock
changes", 2026-08-28) touches both editor/editor_node.cpp and
editor/run/game_view_plugin.cpp -- exactly the two call sites these patches
guard. DROP this patch at the next bump that includes that commit; do NOT
rebase it. Rebasing a mirror of an upstream fix is how a patch outlives the
problem it solved and starts failing to apply.

--- a/editor/run/game_view_plugin.cpp
+++ b/editor/run/game_view_plugin.cpp
@@ -1852,7 +1852,9 @@
 		if (last_editor.is_empty() || (last_editor == "Script" && ScriptEditor::get_singleton()->get_current_layout() == EditorDock::DOCK_LAYOUT_FLOATING)) {
 			CanvasItemEditor::get_singleton()->make_visible();
 		} else {
-			EditorInterface::get_singleton()->set_main_screen_editor(last_editor);
+			EditorDock *dock = EditorNode::get_editor_main_screen()->get_dock_by_name(last_editor);
+			ERR_FAIL_NULL_MSG(dock, "The editor name '" + last_editor + "' was not found.");
+			EditorDockManager::get_singleton()->focus_dock(dock);
 		}
 	}
 }
